      "why": "Fully pipelined gives 1 result/cycle, so throughput = Fmax. To hit 50 MSPS we need Fmax >= 50 MHz. N=12..20 keeps the per-stage logic (one micro-rotation) shallow enough for a high Fmax while N>=12 is the minimum to reach the 2^-12 accuracy floor. data_width 14..18 gives enough output precision (Q1.(W-2)) to keep max_abs_err <= 2^-12 with modest guard bits; W=14 already yields 12 fractional output bits. angle_guard -2..2 and frac_guard 0..2 cover the accuracy knobs that trade a few extra bits (area/power) against error. Rounding fixed to 'round' since it strictly improves accuracy at negligible cost and the spec wants accuracy as the trade-off axis. This is the primary family for the power-vs-accuracy front."
    },
